  "environment_caveats": [
    {
      "id": "lighthouse_desktop_only",
      "description": "DataForSEO Lighthouse runs DESKTOP only (formFactor=desktop, cpuSlowdownMultiplier=1, throughputKbps=10240). Mobile performance typically runs 10-20 points lower. Mobile-specific issues are not surfaced by this audit."
    },
    {
      "id": "mcp_generic_api_request",
      "description": "The dataforseo MCP server exposes only a generic api_request tool, not on_page_lighthouse / on_page_instant_pages. Lighthouse payloads are 0.75-1.05MB each, so this run called /v3/on_page/lighthouse/live/json and /v3/on_page/instant_pages over REST with the DATAFORSEO_* credentials and piped responses to disk. Same account, same data source. Total API cost 0.0408 USD."
    },
    {
      "id": "apex_origin_from_cut_over_at",
      "description": "The client record has no apex_cutover.completed_at key but does carry cut_over_at=2026-05-28T18:48:09Z and deploy_url on the apex. The apex was audited, consistent with the four prior runs. No x-robots-tag noindex header on the apex, so SEO counts toward the verdict."
    },
    {
      "id": "service_area_slot_substituted",
      "description": "/service-areas/madison-al/ still returns 301 to the homepage (re-checked this run), so the service-area slot stays on /service-areas/huntsville-al/, same as the 2026-08-26 run. All six URLs are directly comparable to last month."
    },
    {
      "id": "schema_jsonld_detection",
      "description": "instant_pages reports has_micromarkup=false on all 6 pages, but JSON-LD was re-verified in the served HTML: 3-5 blocks per page, all parse cleanly. has_micromarkup does not count JSON-LD, so missing-schema was NOT flagged."
    },
    {
      "id": "micromarkup_errors_newly_reported",
      "description": "has_micromarkup_errors is set on the 5 pages that carry BreadcrumbList + FAQPage and not on /, which carries neither. The only structural defect found in those blocks is the terminal BreadcrumbList ListItem, which has name and position but no item URL. The block types are the same as last month and the prior run did not record this check, so the flag may reflect a DataForSEO validator change rather than a site change. The same flag appears on the same template shape across several other Rank AI clients this cycle. It is recorded at medium severity per the rubric (schema validation warning), which is what moves these 5 pages from green to amber."
    },
    {
      "id": "render_blocking_dedup",
      "description": "instant_pages sets has_render_blocking_resources=true on all 6 pages. This is the same finding as Lighthouse render-blocking-insight, so it was not recorded a second time as an on-page issue."
    },
    {
      "id": "issue_diff_asymmetry",
      "description": "lighthouse_issues stores the top 5 failing audits per URL. new_issues is computed from the current top 5 against the prior stored set; resolved_issues is computed against the CURRENT FULL failing set, so an issue only counts as resolved if it genuinely no longer fails. Issues that the prior run reported as template issues on 5+ of 6 URLs (cache-insight, image-delivery-insight, network-dependency-tree-insight, render-blocking-insight, unused-javascript, lcp-discovery-insight) are excluded from new_issues, because their absence from the prior per-URL top 5 was a cap artifact, not a real absence."
    },
